{
  "name": "llm-det (llm backends dashboard + settings panel, operator vs builder, seeded 3 backends, add/edit/delete dialogs cancelled, provider-select reveal, cost ceiling strip, network actions reduced to boundaries)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "LlmBackendCard.svelte no longer suffixes its ids with the backend name: llm-backend-card, llm-backend-badge, set-default, llm-backend-ping-btn, edit-backend, delete-backend are plain and repeated per card, so they are targeted by testid + nth instead of testidPrefix.",
    "set-default / llm-backend-ping-btn / edit-backend / delete-backend live in the builderActions snippet, so they render in builder mode only; the settings walk runs after the mode is switched to builder. set-default additionally renders only on a non-default backend.",
    "llm-dialog-enabled-switch and llm-dialog-default-switch are the <button role=switch> a SettingsToggle composes off llm-dialog-enabled / llm-dialog-default (SettingsToggle.svelte:53 passes `${dataTestId}-switch` to Toggle.svelte, which spreads it onto the button, :47-63). The earlier note claiming the inner ids resolve to nothing was wrong; llm-advanced-det drives them by their exact ids.",
    "llm-dialog-browse is played through a stubbed picker: handleBrowse (LlmBackendDialog.svelte:72-93) calls plugin-dialog `open`, which is the IPC plugin:dialog|open; the stub resolves ${HOME}/.apollia/models/Phi-3-mini-Q4.gguf (a seed file, tests/cli/seed/files/models) once, and applySelectedPath (:115-124) writes it into form.model. The dialog is cancelled afterwards, nothing persisted.",
    "llm-dialog-test on the ADD path is a pure local validation (handleTest :156-169, `!editing` branch): with name/endpoint/apikey/model filled the form has no errors, so the click renders llm-dialog-test-result without any network call. On the EDIT path the same button pings the backend, which is why it is only played here.",
    "llm-error-details-toggle: set-default on the DISABLED seeded openai-gpt4o-mini (system.sql enabled=0). set_default itself succeeds (apollia-core llm_backend.rs:398-420 only refuses an unknown name), then reload_llm_from_db (commands/llm.rs:378-443) rebuilds the router from enabled configs only (router/construct.rs:222) and resolve_default_backend refuses a default that is not instantiated (router/backends.rs:262-275), so the command rejects before swapping the router; handleSetDefault's catch (settings/Llm.svelte:80-82) sets actionError, humanize keeps the raw string as detail (humanize.ts:261-274) and LlmActionErrorBanner mounts the Disclosure whose header composes llm-error-details-toggle (Disclosure.svelte:75). Cards are ORDER BY name (llm_backend.rs:286) and set-default renders on non-default cards only (LlmBackendCard.svelte:181), so after 11c the four cards are anthropic-claude (default), automation-saved, local-llama-server, openai-gpt4o-mini and set-default nth 2 is the disabled one. The restore is two clicks (nth 1 then nth 0) because the list may or may not have been refreshed by the llm-changed SSE the failed reload emits (sse.ts:595-605): on a stale list nth 1 is local-llama-server, on a refreshed one automation-saved; both succeed, both refresh, and on the refreshed list nth 0 is anthropic-claude either way, which is the state llm-det already leaves.",
    "llm-backend-ping-btn is played in the settings list through a stubbed IPC: handlePing -> pingLlmBackend -> ping_llm_backend (LlmBackendCard.svelte:75-97, ipc/llm.ts:21-23) sends a real completion through the router with no handler-side timeout, and nth 0 is anthropic-claude, a remote backend with a placeholder key, so the real outcome depends on the network. The block after 07-settings-cards-controls stubs the command twice, once each: a resolve shaped like PingResult (commands/llm.rs:98-107, available:true latency_ms:42) renders llm-ping-result with llm.ping_ok, asserted by 'Ping OK (42ms)', which is the same string in both locales; then a reject with a raw string lands in the catch and is rendered verbatim as pingError on the same anchor. The card clears the feedback after FEEDBACK_MS (5 s, :41), so the assertions sit right after each click. The command is cleared afterwards; nothing is written. On the llm page (04-llm-builder-cards-ping-boundary) the button is still only asserted."
  ],
